# /sdd-skills

Purpose:
  Discover, map, and recommend skills from the .sdd/skills/ ecosystem.
  Makes the 80+ skill files queryable and connects them to pending tasks
  and project context.

Owns: commands/sdd-skills.sdd

Description:
  Reads .sdd/skills/INDEX.sdd and all subdirectories to produce a
  skill catalog. Lists skills by category, language, framework,
  database, and platform. Shows skill coverage for the current project
  and recommends skills for pending tasks based on task metadata
  and existing decisions.

Usage:
  /sdd-skills
  /sdd-skills --category <category>
  /sdd-skills --language <language>
  /sdd-skills --framework <framework>
  /sdd-skills --recommend
  /sdd-skills --coverage
  /sdd-skills --json

Options:
  --category   Filter by category (languages, frameworks, databases, platforms, cross-cutting)
  --language   Filter by programming language (go, python, rust, java, etc.)
  --framework  Filter by framework (react, django, spring-boot, etc.)
  --recommend  Recommend skills for pending tasks
  --coverage   Show skill coverage for current project
  --json       Output machine-readable JSON

Mode: READ_ONLY

SkillCategories:
  languages:
    go, rust, java, php, python, csharp, cpp, typescript, javascript, swift, kotlin, ruby
  frameworks:
    react, flutter, react-native, swiftui, kotlin-multiplatform, nextjs, nestjs, spring-boot, django, fastapi, express, dotnet, laravel, symfony, svelte
  databases:
    postgresql, mongodb, redis, mysql, cassandra, elasticsearch
  platforms:
    docker, kubernetes, aws, gcp, azure, terraform
  cross-cutting:
    testing, security, architecture, observability
  meta:
    sdd, skills, engineering, devops, messaging

Output:
  SKILL CATALOG

    Total Skills:       <count>
    Categories:         <count>
    Languages:          <count>
    Frameworks:         <count>
    Databases:          <count>
    Platforms:          <count>
    Cross-Cutting:      <count>

  Skills by Category:
    [languages]
      go/        L1-L5 skill files
      python/    L1-L5 skill files
      ...

  Project Coverage:
    [covered]   go, python, docker, postgresql
    [missing]   rust, kafka, aws

  Recommendations:
    [REC-001] language: go | reason: pending task T204 uses Go
    [REC-002] framework: django | reason: project uses Python web stack

Rules:
  [SKL-01] /sdd-skills MUST NOT modify any file.
  [SKL-02] Skill listing MUST include competency level (L1-L5) when present.
  [SKL-03] Recommendations MUST be derived from pending tasks and project decisions.
  [SKL-04] Missing coverage MUST be flagged for human review.
  [SKL-05] Skill categories MUST match .sdd/skills/ directory structure.

Navigation:
   INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
   SkillsIndex: @../skills/INDEX.sdd
   SkillsRoot: @../skills/
   CrossCutting: @../skills/cross-cutting/INDEX.sdd
   Tasks: @../tasks/INDEX.sdd
   Decisions: @../decisions/INDEX.sdd
   Projects: @../projects/INDEX.sdd

State: +
